            "review_title": "Review at Baieta Saigon",
            "review_text": "Xpatxplorer\nNew Delhi, India811 contributions\n1\nTapas & pizza\nSep 2023 • Friends\nYou know you’ve hit gold while trying a new restaurant when your table checks opening hours for brunch/breakfast, happy hours and starts making plans for the next visit. Plans were being made to come back with the missing teen, birthday parties being discussed and what not. Thankyou Jerome Buzenet for pointing us to @baieta restaurant saison. Please keep your reviews coming!\nExcellent view, great vibe and delicious food. We ordered plenty and weren’t disappointed by a single dish. We started with tapas/ appetizers including crispy brie, crispy quail, truffle ham, tuna and prawn ceviche and grilled asparagus. Ended with a delicious wood fired pizza. The burgers looked great and were noted for next time:) \nThis place is located on the river in the same bit as Chang's Bistro & Cakes, 2 restaurants with really good food and priced at a point you can keep going back without too much thought.\nThey are very new so be a little patient with the service and I would avoid large complicated group orders till they settle down. I’m sure they will sort it all out very quickly with the presence of the owner/partners on the floor keeping a keen eye on every table.\nWe got into a lovely chat with the amicable Florian who obviously has a stake. While he did buy us a round of drinks,this review was already decided and the conversation was congratulatory!\nVegetarians there are a few options which sounded delicious. \nWishing team Baieta Restaurant Saigon the very best.\nRead more\nWritten September 25, 2023",
